<p>Simbi: Bedtime Stories ("Simbi", "we", "us", or "our") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and share information when you use our mobile application, website, and related services (together, the "Services").</p>

<p>If you do not agree with this Privacy Policy, please do not use the Services.</p>

<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
<div class="contact-block">
	<span class="contact-name">Matthew Smart</span>
	<span>Email: <a href="mailto:support@getsimbi.com">support@getsimbi.com</a></span>
	<span>Website: <a href="https://getsimbi.com">getsimbi.com</a></span>
</div>

<h2>2. Who this policy applies to</h2>
<p>Simbi is designed for use by parents or guardians for their family, including children using the app under adult supervision. We aim to collect only the information reasonably necessary to provide the Services.</p>

<h2>3. Information we collect</h2>
<p>We may collect the following categories of information:</p>

<h3>A. Account and family information</h3>
<p>We may collect information needed to create, manage, and support your use of Simbi, such as:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Parent or guardian name</li>
	<li>Email address</li>
	<li>Family account identifiers</li>
	<li>Authentication identifiers</li>
	<li>Join codes used to connect devices or family members</li>
	<li>Subscription or entitlement status</li>
</ul>

<h3>B. Child profile information</h3>
<p>If you create a child profile in the app, we may collect information a parent or guardian chooses to provide, such as:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Child nickname or first name</li>
	<li>Age or age range</li>
	<li>Avatar or character selections</li>
	<li>Story preferences, themes, helpers, favourites, or related settings</li>
</ul>
<p>Please do not provide sensitive personal information about a child.</p>

<h3>C. Story generation and app content</h3>
<p>To provide the core features of Simbi, we may process:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Prompts you submit</li>
	<li>Character details you enter</li>
	<li>Story settings and preferences</li>
	<li>Generated stories</li>
	<li>Audio playback preferences</li>
	<li>Saved stories, library items, and related in-app content</li>
</ul>

<h3>D. Purchase and subscription information</h3>
<p>If you subscribe or make purchases, payment processing is handled by Apple. We do not receive your full payment card details. We may receive information such as:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Subscription tier</li>
	<li>Product purchased</li>
	<li>Entitlement status</li>
	<li>Renewal, expiration, billing issue, or cancellation status</li>
	<li>Transaction or subscription identifiers</li>
</ul>

<h3>E. Device, diagnostics, and usage information</h3>
<p>We may automatically collect limited technical and app-related information such as:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Device type</li>
	<li>Operating system</li>
	<li>App version</li>
	<li>Crash diagnostics</li>
	<li>Performance and reliability information</li>
	<li>Basic usage information needed to operate, maintain, and improve the Services</li>
</ul>

<h3>F. Support communications</h3>
<p>If you contact us for support or send us a message, we may collect:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Your name</li>
	<li>Email address</li>
	<li>The contents of your message</li>
	<li>Any attachments, screenshots, or information you choose to send</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. How we use information</h2>
<p>We use information to:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Provide, operate, and maintain Simbi</li>
	<li>Create and deliver personalised bedtime stories and audio</li>
	<li>Support family accounts, child profiles, and connected devices</li>
	<li>Maintain subscriptions and entitlements</li>
	<li>Save story history and preferences</li>
	<li>Improve app performance, reliability, and safety</li>
	<li>Respond to support requests and user enquiries</li>
	<li>Prevent fraud, abuse, or misuse of the Services</li>
	<li>Comply with legal and regulatory obligations</li>
	<li>Enforce our terms, policies, and other agreements</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Legal bases for processing</h2>
<p>Where applicable under UK GDPR and similar laws, we process personal data on one or more of the following legal bases:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Performance of a contract</li>
	<li>Legitimate interests</li>
	<li>Consent</li>
	<li>Compliance with legal obligations</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. How we share information</h2>
<p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
<p>We may share information with trusted service providers only as reasonably necessary to operate, provide, secure, and improve the Services. These may include providers that help us with:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Cloud hosting and database infrastructure</li>
	<li>Authentication and account services</li>
	<li>Crash reporting, diagnostics, and technical support</li>
	<li>Subscription and purchase infrastructure</li>
	<li>AI story generation and voice or audio generation</li>
	<li>Customer support tools</li>
</ul>
<p>These providers may process information on our behalf and only as needed to provide services to us, subject to appropriate contractual or legal safeguards where required.</p>
<p>We may also disclose information:</p>
<ul>
	<li>If required by law, regulation, legal process, or governmental request</li>
	<li>To protect the rights, property, or safety of users, our business, or others</li>
	<li>In connection with a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganisation, sale of assets, or similar business transaction</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. AI-generated content</h2>
<p>Simbi may use third-party AI and voice providers to generate story text, narration, and related features.</p>
<p>Information submitted for story creation, such as child profile details, prompts, character selections, and story preferences, may be processed by those providers solely to generate the requested content and to maintain, secure, and troubleshoot those services, subject to their applicable terms and privacy practices.</p>

<h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
<p>We take children's privacy seriously.</p>
<p>Simbi is intended to be used by a parent or guardian for their family, or with appropriate parental involvement. We do not knowingly collect more personal information from children than is reasonably necessary for the functionality of the Services.</p>
<p>Parents or guardians are responsible for deciding what information they choose to provide about a child.</p>
<p>Parents or guardians may contact us to:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Request access to personal data associated with their account</li>
	<li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
	<li>Request deletion of account, child profile, or related data</li>
</ul>
<p>If you believe a child's information has been provided inappropriately, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@getsimbi.com">support@getsimbi.com</a>.</p>

<h2>9. Data retention</h2>
<p>We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary to:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Provide and maintain the Services</li>
	<li>Maintain your account and saved content</li>
	<li>Comply with legal, tax, accounting, or regulatory obligations</li>
	<li>Resolve disputes</li>
	<li>Enforce our agreements</li>
</ul>
<p>If you request deletion, we will delete or anonymise your information unless we are legally required or otherwise permitted to retain certain data.</p>

<h2>10. Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights to:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Access your personal data</li>
	<li>Correct inaccurate data</li>
	<li>Request deletion of your data</li>
	<li>Object to certain processing</li>
	<li>Restrict certain processing</li>
	<li>Request portability of your data</li>
	<li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li>
</ul>
<p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@getsimbi.com">support@getsimbi.com</a>.</p>

<h2>11. Data deletion and privacy choices</h2>
<p>You can request deletion of your account, child profiles, saved stories, or make other privacy-related requests by:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Using any deletion feature available within the app, where provided</li>
	<li>Contacting us at <a href="mailto:support@getsimbi.com">support@getsimbi.com</a></li>
</ul>
<p>We will respond within a reasonable timeframe and in accordance with applicable law.</p>

<h2>12. International data transfers</h2>
<p>Your information may be processed in countries outside your country of residence. Where required, we take reasonable steps to ensure that appropriate safeguards are in place for such transfers.</p>

<h2>13. Security</h2>
<p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures designed to protect personal information. However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

<h2>14. Third-party services and links</h2>
<p>The Services may rely on, integrate with, or link to third-party services. Those third parties operate under their own terms and privacy policies, and we are not responsible for their independent privacy practices.</p>

<h2>15. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we will update the "Last updated" date and may provide additional notice where appropriate.</p>

<h2>16. Contact us</h2>
<p>If you have any questions, privacy requests, or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, contact:</p>
